From 6ba7de36ee008f6ba10b7485bcd6a040b94456ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 04:31:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] NEMO's TKE scheme as a vertical mixing option ([ocean]
 closure = "NEMO"), for the comparison with GLORYS
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

nemo_tke_vertical_diffusivity.jl: the base scheme of NEMO's zdftke.F90 (reference namelist, no Langmuir
or penetration terms) as a flavour of CATKEVerticalDiffusivity; the same file as Oceananigans branch
fjp/nemo-tke (patch 084), loaded into Oceananigans once per Julia process unless the installed
Oceananigans has it, so no change to the Manifest.
panarctic.jl: closure = "NEMO", with [ocean] nemo_surface_tke (rn_ebb, 67.83) and
nemo_convective_diffusivity (rn_evd, 100 m²/s); catke_under_ice refused with it.
under_ice_coupling.jl: the under-ice TKE flux override, which stays loaded in a reused process, reads
Cᵂu★ only from CATKE's own TKE equation (NEMO's has none).
Configs: smoke test (100 km, 4 days) and NEMO twins of the 20 Nov baseline at 50 and 100 levels.

Untested: Claude cannot run Julia.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AbhhvoXen2vZSP4ZrEkbYa
